    "problem": {
      "type": "dh-media-text",
      "blocks": {
        "p1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Very dry, sensitive skin struggles to hold on to water. In Singapore it gets worse, with aircon all day and heat and sweat outside. Your face goes tight, then flaky.</p><p>So you try a cream. Some sting. Some smell. Some sit so heavy you can't put make-up on top. One by one, they end up in a drawer.</p><p>Your skin isn't being difficult. Most creams just weren't made for it.</p>"
          }
        },
