    "ice_plant": {
      "type": "dh-media-text",
      "blocks": {
        "p1": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The ice plant grows in dry, salty ground. It survives by storing water in tiny balloon-like cells on its leaves. They glitter like ice, which is how it got its name.</p><p>This cream uses that plant's juice as its third ingredient, after water and jojoba oil. Then it adds avocado, almond and sunflower oils and shea, mango and cocoa butters. Those sit on your skin and help keep the water there.</p><p>No perfume is added. You can read every ingredient further down.</p>"
          }
        },
        "b1": {
          "type": "button",
